# ACCEPTANCE: cu-002

Criterion 3 -- workers overlap. With enrichment running against a backlog:

  pgrep -fc "opencode run"

Expected: 4 or more while a batch is in flight, sampled several times.

Criterion 4 -- attempts are bounded. Point the model at one opencode does not
serve, by putting this line in .env:

  NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_MODEL=opencode/muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free

Start enrichment. Expected: each item is attempted 3 times, warned on each
failure with "attempt N of 3", then skipped once, with one skip line naming the
item. Restore .env afterwards.

Criterion 5 -- an exhausted item does not block the queue. Same run. Expected: the
pipeline keeps printing poll lines on successive polls, the offset advances, and
no poll waits forever.

Criterion 6 -- the poll line reports counts:

  grep -E "poll merged [0-9]+ enriched units \([0-9]+ enriched, [0-9]+ failed\)"

Expected: matching lines during a live run.

Criterion 7 -- startup refuses a dead model. With the same bogus .env line, start
enrichment. Expected: readiness reports not-ready naming the model, Main logs
"startup aborted", and the process exits non-zero before any poll line. Remove the
bogus line afterwards.

Criterion 8 -- no regression:

  cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt compile
  cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt test

Expected: clean compile, all tests green, including MergeBackfillSpec.

The Advisor does not run sbt; these two probes are the code lead's.
